{{Endplainlist}}|website=|website_title=Official website|italic_title=no|native_name=|inspired_by={{W|Sanremo Music Festival}}|caption=[[Piauca Arena]] (in [[Macaio]]), which hosted the 2025 Festival de Canarias}}'''Festival de Canarias''' ({{W|IPA|fɨʃtiˈval dɐ kɐ̃ˈsɐ̃w|lang}}; "[[W:Domestic canary|Canary]] Festival"; '''FdC''') is the name given to the most popular n national festival, produced and broadcast by [[Rádio e Televisão de Balisca|Rádio y Television de Balisca]] (RTB) first held in 1964. 

Since 2019 it has been the national selection event to determine the Balisca entry for the [[AINVision Song Contest]]. However, unlike other competitions elsewhere, like Sweden's [[W:Melodifestivalen|Melodifestivalen]], this is only a secondary purpose of the festival, and winners of FdC are given [[W:Right of first refusal|right of first refusal]] in regards to their AINVision participation.

